        713.54831999999999,
        136.17176400000005,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "II. Basis for Jurisdiction"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.98,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        74.883420000000001,
        688.16255999999998,
        469.69914600000027,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "Federal courts are courts of limited jurisdiction (limited power). Generally, only two types of cases can be"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.98,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        74.883420000000001,
        675.43673999999999,
        470.73895200000015,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "heard in federal court: cases involving a federal question and cases involving diversity of citizenship of the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.98,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        74.883420000000029,
        662.71091999999999,
        486.5062320000003,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "parties. Under 28 U.S.C. § 1331, a case arising under the United States Constitution or federal laws or treaties"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.98,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        74.883420000000058,
        649.98509999999999,
        466.17786000000007,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "is a federal question case. Under 28 U.S.C. § 1332, a case in which a citizen of one State sues a citizen of"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.98,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        74.883420000000058,
        637.25927999999999,
        470.33269200000012,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "another State or nation and the amount at stake is more than $75,000 is a diversity of citizenship case. In a"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.98,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        74.883420000000058,
        624.53345999999999,
        409.36404600000054,
        12.154859999999985
      ],
      "text" : "diversity of citizenship case, no defendant may be a citizen of the same State as any plaintiff."
    },
